      "side": 0,
      "message": "It the initial version of aosp/3632018 mp_state was checked regardless, then I changed it to the current state in https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3632018/3..4/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c#b762. But the only reason for that was just a stupid speculative micro-optimization: kvm_vcpu_is_reset_bsp() (called by pkvm_vcpu_is_pvmfw_bsp()) is not an inline function, so this avoided calling it every time a vCPU is run. Logically it was still correct, since we never changed mp_state of an already running vCPU.\n\nNow, we do change mp_state in case of a triple fault, so we need to check mp_state regardless. And we still check kvm_vcpu_has_run() before calling kvm_vcpu_is_reset_bsp() anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "cb9432b7_91123972",
      "revId": "d57dbce9c3a8e544346764c9c2f3e7675999c97c",
